    {
      "text": "A successful response returns code 200. To learn more, see API Response Codes and Error Messages."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Updating an AppProtection Policy Rule",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To update the details of an AppProtection policy rule in the policy set:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Get the policySetId captured in Prerequisite API Call.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Use the JSON payload from Creating a New AppProtection Rule and send a PUT request to the following endpoint: /mgmtconfig/v2/admin/customers/{customerId}/policySet/{policySetId}/rule/{ruleId}.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "Provide the following values in the request endpoint:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "customerId: The ZPA tenant ID of the customer.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "policySetId: The ID of the inspection policy set captured in the Prerequisite API Call section.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "ruleId: The ID of the inspection rule.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "For example: /mgmtconfig/v2/admin/customers/72057615512764416/policySet/72057615512764421/rule/72057615512764641.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "View the JSON payload",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "{ \"policySetId\": \"<policySetId>\", \"id\": \"<ruleId>\", \"conditions\": [ { \"operands\": [ { \"objectType\": \"APP\", \"values\": [ \"<applicationId>\", \"<applicationId>\", \"<applicationId>\" ] }, { \"objectType\": \"APP_GROUP\", \"values\": [ \"<segmentGroupId>\" ] } ] } ], \"name\": \"<example Policy Rule Name>\", \"description\": \"<Example Policy Rule Description>\", \"action\": \"INSPECT\", \"zpnInspectionProfileId\": \"<AppProtectionProfileId>\" }",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "A successful response yields code 204, meaning the AppProtection rule is updated. To learn more, see API Response Codes and Error Messages."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Updating a Rule Order",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To update a rule order:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Send a PUT request to the following endpoint: /mgmtconfig/v1/admin/customers/{customerId}/policySet/{policySetId}/rule/{ruleId}/reorder/{newOrder}.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Provide the following parameters in the request endpoint:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "customerId: The ZPA tenant ID of the customer.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "policySetId: The ID of the policy set.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "ruleId: The ID of the AppProtection rule.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "newOrder: The new order of the rule.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "For example: /mgmtconfig/v1/admin/customers/72057594037927936/policySet/72057594037938994/rule/72057615512764641/reorder/4."
    },
    {
      "text": "A successful response returns code 204, meaning the rule order is updated. To learn more, see API Response Codes and Error Messages."
    },
    {
      "text": "The ability to update the rule order for all rules in a policy set is also available. To learn more, see Configuring Access Policies Using API."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Deleting an AppProtection Rule",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To delete an AppProtection rule:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Send a DELETE request to the following endpoint: /mgmtconfig/v1/admin/customers/{customerId}/policySet/{policySetId}/rule/{ruleId}.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Provide the following values in the request endpoint:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "customerId: The ZPA tenant ID of the customer.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "policySetId: The ID of the AppProtection policy set captured in the Prerequisite API Call section.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "ruleId: The ID of the rule you created in Create a New Inspection Rule.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "For example: /mgmtconfig/v1/admin/customers/72057615512764416/policySet/72057615512764421/rule/72057615512764641."
    },
    {
      "text": "A successful response yields code 204, meaning the AppProtection rule is deleted. To learn more, see API Response Codes and Error Messages."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Getting Details of All Client Types",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To get details of all client types:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Send a GET request to the following endpoint: /mgmtconfig/v1/admin/customers/{customerId}/clientTypes.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Provide the customerId, the ZPA tenant ID of the customer, in the request endpoint. For example: /mgmtconfig/v1/admin/customers/217246660302995456/clientTypes.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "View an example response",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "{",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "\"zpn_client_type_exporter\": \"Web Browser\",",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "\"zpn_client_type_exporter_noauth\": \"Web Browser Unauthenticated\",",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "\"zpn_client_type_machine_tunnel\": \"Machine Tunnel\",",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "\"zpn_client_type_edge_connector\": \"Cloud Connector\",",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "\"zpn_client_type_zia_inspection\": \"ZIA Inspection\",",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "\"zpn_client_type_zapp\": \"Client Connector\",",
      "depth": 0
